---
import { pageUrl } from "../../data/pages";
import Puerta from "../../components/Puerta.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout lang="en" page="manifesto">
<section class="hero manifesto-hero reveal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Manifesto</h1>
      <p class="lead">Why Atarazana Founder House exists, who it is for and how we want it to work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="toc reveal" aria-label="Contents">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="toc-head"><span>Contents</span><span>8 chapters</span></div>
      <ol class="toc-list">
        <li><a href="#malaga">They were already building here</a></li>
        <li><a href="#work">What you do, not how you pitch it</a></li>
        <li><a href="#formats">What happens at each meetup</a></li>
        <li><a href="#who">Who gets in and why</a></li>
        <li><a href="#rules">Our rules</a></li>
        <li><a href="#not">What we do not do</a></li>
        <li><a href="#name">Why this name</a></li>
        <li><a href="#community">A community, not a venue</a></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter reveal" id="malaga">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>They were already building here</h2>
      <blockquote class="pull chapter-quote">In the 14th century, Málaga built ships. <strong>Today it builds technology.</strong></blockquote>
      <p>Behind the gate that now leads into the Atarazanas Market, Málaga spent centuries building the ships that crossed the Mediterranean. Today the city has startups, universities, technical talent, investment, accelerators and a tech hub that keeps growing. That work is already done, and it was no accident.</p>
      <p>What we missed was a shared workshop: a place where people who build could get together regularly, without waiting for the next big date and without catching a plane. A place for the unplanned conversation, the prototype shown too early and the idea several people decide to build together.</p>
      <p>Atarazana Founder House fills that gap: small, regular meetups where the people building in Málaga actually get to know each other.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter band reveal" id="work">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you do, not how you pitch it</h2>
      <blockquote class="pull chapter-quote">What matters here is what you build, <strong>not how you present it.</strong></blockquote>
      <p>Atarazana Founder House is designed for the people who do the work. What counts is what you are trying to build, what you learned along the way and how much you share it. Job title, company and follower count stay outside.</p>
      <p>We like people who show what they do: code, product, architecture, mistakes and awkward questions. A half-finished launch makes for a better conversation than a polished success story.</p>
      <ul class="principles-list">
        <li>A demo is worth more than a pitch.</li>
        <li>One hard decision is worth more than ten generic tips.</li>
        <li>An honest question is worth more than a business card.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter reveal" id="formats">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What happens at each meetup</h2>
      <blockquote class="pull chapter-quote">A few talks. <strong>Plenty of time to talk.</strong></blockquote>
      <p>At each marea, a few people who are building share what they do, what they have learned and what they still have not figured out. Then there is food, drinks and plenty of time to keep the conversation going with whoever just presented or whoever is next to you.</p>
      <p>The programme matters less than what happens around it: the unplanned conversation and what comes out of it. <a href={`${pageUrl("en", "index")}#session`}>Here is the programme for the next marea</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter band reveal" id="who">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Who gets in and why</h2>
      <blockquote class="pull chapter-quote">Who gets in depends on <strong>what you bring</strong>, not your job title.</blockquote>
      <p>We ask for invites to protect what happens inside. We want every person who comes in to make the conversation better, and that is enough: anyone who is building something and has something to contribute gets in.</p>
      <p>We look for a mix of founders, engineers, research, product and design people, exceptional students and profiles that are hard to label. People with a track record and people who are not known yet but are already doing great work.</p>
      <p>Every meetup keeps room for new faces. You become part of the community by coming, coming back and helping others.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter reveal" id="rules">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Our rules</h2>
      <div class="rules-grid">
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>Show your work</h3><p>If you can show it working, do not just tell it with slides.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>No theatre</h3><p>Talks and direct conversation. There is always room for the hard question.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>Work before title</h3><p>What you have built matters more than how your title looks on LinkedIn.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>Unfinished is welcome</h3><p>Half-done work makes for better conversations than a closed success story.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>Give before you ask</h3><p>Introduce two people, share what you know, unblock someone.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>Selective, but open</h3><p>We look after who is in the room and always keep space for new talent.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>What is said, stays</h3><p>Whoever shares something decides whether it can leave the room.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><h3>Partners do not decide</h3><p>Partners make each meetup possible, but they do not choose who gets in, who speaks or what is discussed.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter band reveal" id="not">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <p>No forced networking games, no business-card rounds, no sales talks. If a conversation needs a game to get started, it probably was not going to be a good one. We set up the conditions and step aside:</p>
      <ul class="principles-list">
        <li>A shared table.</li>
        <li>An honest demo.</li>
        <li>A drink after the last talk.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We are not here to replace anyone. We build on the work of those who have been moving the Málaga ecosystem for years and add something smaller, more frequent and focused on builders.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter reveal" id="name">
    <div class="wrap why-grid">
      <div>
        <h2>Why this name</h2>
        <blockquote class="pull chapter-quote">Different tools, <strong>same attitude.</strong></blockquote>
        <Puerta caption="Gate of the Atarazanas · 14th c. · 36.7202° N / 4.4214° W" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The Atarazanas were Málaga’s shipyards in Nasrid times: the place where the ships that crossed the Mediterranean were built. Workshop work, no stage. The gate of that building still stands and is now the entrance to the Atarazanas Market.</p>
        <p>The word comes from Andalusi Arabic <em>dār aṣ-ṣināʿa</em>, “house of industry”: the place where things are made. The same word, by way of Venetian, gave English <em>arsenal</em>.</p>
        <p>We care about that attitude, not nostalgia: making things by hand, experimenting, mixing and creating without asking for permission. Today that energy is in the people building products, companies and technology from here. The material changed. The attitude is the same.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter band reveal" id="community">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>A community, not a venue</h2>
      <blockquote class="pull chapter-quote">Atarazana Founder House is <strong>the people who come back.</strong></blockquote>
      <p>We have no fixed venue. Each meetup happens in a different place in Málaga and, when the night ends, what remains are the relationships, the products that were shown, the conversations still open and the things that start being built afterwards.</p>
      <p>We want to be the place you come back to: where a conversation turns into a company, a demo finds its first customer and an idea finds its first engineer. See you inside.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
